# Steamworks: SteamPipe build scripts

app_build and depot_build scripts must point to folders that exist, list depots that have a script, never set the default branch live (Valve only allows that by hand in Steamworks) and never ship steam_appid.txt.

## steam_appid.txt is in a build folder (warning)

- Why: steam_appid.txt is for development. In a shipped build it makes SteamAPI_RestartAppIfNecessary skip the relaunch through Steam, so the game can start without Steam's checks.
- Fix: Leave steam_appid.txt out of the build folders and depots you upload.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/api#SteamAPI_RestartAppIfNecessary

## A build script sets the default branch live (error)

- Why: Valve does not let build scripts set the default branch live; that is done by hand in Steamworks.
- Fix: Set a beta branch in "setlive" (or leave it empty) and set the default branch live in Steamworks.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/uploading

## A build script points to something that does not exist (error)

- Why: steamcmd stops, or uploads an empty or wrong depot, when a content root, file mapping or depot script is missing.
- Fix: Fix the path in the script, or build the game into that folder first.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/uploading

With the steamworks-mcp server connected, `check_code(path)` finds these problems in the whole project, with file and line (`check_code(path, rules=["steamworks-build-scripts"])` for this group only).
